# HTML and CSS conventions

cha.mdc is authoritative on colors, tokens and the blocked hex list.
Never write a raw hex value. All colors flow through css/tokens.css as
--cha-* variables, and scripts/verify.js enforces it. Do not bypass it.

To match the theme, read the token the surrounding component already
uses. Do not introduce a new value, and do not copy a hex out of a design
note into a stylesheet.

## Placement

- New or changed CSS goes in an override block at the very BOTTOM of the
  existing <style> block in index.html, or the bottom of the target
  stylesheet. Do not edit rules above that point unless the user asked
  for that exact rule to change.
- Before adding a rule, search EVERY stylesheet in the repo for an
  existing rule on the same selector. Cross-stylesheet collisions are a
  repeat failure here, and your own diff will not reveal one. Checking
  only the file you edited is not sufficient.
- Namespace new class names.

## HTML

- Do not change structure, copy, colour, spacing, font or layout unless
  that is the requested change.
- Load order in index.html is fixed. See cha.mdc. Do not reorder, do not
  add defer.

## Accessibility floor

Interactive elements reachable by keyboard. Any control conveying state
needs a text label, not colour alone. Agents read this while typing on a
live call.
